#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bin/ubx-secrets -- the secrets primitive's convergence PLANNER, plus a
thin `observe` subcommand (SPEC.md §8.1 "Secrets (decided design)", §6,
§4.3 "Switching and convergence" -- "none" downtime; GitHub issue #78,
milestone M4). THE foundational secrets primitive: git-crypt onboarding
(#79), password-hash consumption (#80), and the Pro token (#82) all source
from what this script + nix/secrets.nix + bin/ubx-secrets-apply establish.

-- Why this lives outside Nix, as a script under bin/ ----------------------

Exactly bin/ubx-users' own reasoning (see that script's header): convergence
is a function of REAL, observed system state (what is actually materialized
under /run/secrets right now), which Nix's build graph has no business
seeing. nix/secrets.nix owns the declaration surface and renders it to a
flat JSON manifest (see that file's header for the schema); this script
CONSUMES that manifest plus a fixture (in tests) or real (`observe`, at
activation) copy of /run/secrets' own state and decides what needs to
change. Kept pure Python specifically so the planner half is unit-testable
with zero root, network, or `nix` binary -- see tests/unit/160-16x.

-- The two subcommands ------------------------------------------------------

  ubx-secrets plan --manifest FILE --observed FILE [--out FILE]
    Pure function of its inputs: declared manifest + observed /run/secrets
    state -> a deterministic JSON PLAN on stdout (or --out). Never touches a
    real system.

  ubx-secrets observe [--run-secrets-dir DIR] [--manifest FILE] [--mounts-file FILE] [--out FILE]
    Walks a real (or, in tests, temp) /run/secrets directory and emits its
    observed-state JSON in the exact shape `plan` consumes. `--manifest` is
    optional: when given, every declared secret whose effective `dst`
    differs from its own canonical `/run/secrets/<name>` copy (SPEC.md
    §8.1's symlink case) is additionally checked for its CURRENT resolved
    symlink target, so `plan` can tell an already-correct symlink from one
    that still needs (re)creating (see "The observed schema" below,
    `symlinkTarget`). Omitted entirely, no symlink is ever ADDITIONALLY
    checked outside `--run-secrets-dir` itself (a `plan` run against that
    thinner observed state simply always (re)plans every custom-dst
    secret's symlink -- see `plan`'s own comment on `symlink.create` for why
    that is still correct, just not maximally quiet).

-- The manifest schema (produced by nix/secrets.nix's `renderManifestJSON`) -

  {
    "version": 1,
    "secrets": [
      { "name": ..., "owner": "root", "group": "root", "mode": "0400",
        "dst": "/run/secrets/<name>", "environmentVariable": <str|null> },
      ...
    ]
  }
`dst` is always the EFFECTIVE delivery path (SPEC.md §8.1's own
`secrets.<name>.path`) -- either a declared custom path, or the default
`/run/secrets/<name>` tmpfs path nix/secrets.nix's own render already
applied. See that file's header, "THE ABSOLUTE INVARIANT": this manifest
NEVER carries a `src` field or any secret material -- only the six keys
above. `validate_manifest` below defense-in-depth REJECTS a manifest secret
object carrying ANY other key at all (not just tolerating/ignoring it) --
see tests/unit/160-secrets-purity-guard.sh, which asserts exactly this.

-- The canonical-copy model (SPEC.md §8.1) ----------------------------------

Every declared secret's real material is materialized EXACTLY ONCE, at its
own canonical path `/run/secrets/<name>` (tmpfs, owner/group/mode from the
manifest) -- regardless of `dst`. When `dst` differs from that canonical
path (a custom `dst`, e.g. `/etc/wireguard/wg0.key`), delivery ADDITIONALLY
creates `dst` as a SYMLINK to the canonical copy ("Setting `dst` places the
secret (as a symlink to the managed material) at a fixed path for software
that demands one"). This is why `plan`'s output below is split into
`materialize` (the one real, owned copy at `/run/secrets/<name>`) and
`symlink` (the optional extra pointer at a custom `dst`) -- exactly two
independent, separately-diffable concerns.

-- The observed schema ------------------------------------------------------

  {
    "version": 1,
    "entries": [
      { "name": ..., "owner": ..., "group": ..., "mode": ...,
        "envVar": <str|null>, "symlinkTarget": <str|null> },
      ...
    ]
  }
One entry per file currently found directly under the observed
`/run/secrets/` directory (excluding any `<name>.env` sibling, which is
folded into that base entry's own `envVar` field instead -- see `observe`'s
own docstring for exactly how that value is read). `symlinkTarget` is only
ever meaningful for a secret this run also knows (via `--manifest`) has a
custom `dst`; it is the CURRENT resolved target of that `dst` path if it is
already a symlink, else null (this is what makes an already-converged
custom-`dst` secret plan to a real no-op -- see `plan`'s own comment).

-- The plan schema ----------------------------------------------------------

  {
    "version": 1,
    "empty": <bool>,
    "materialize": {
      "create": [ { "name", "dst", "owner", "group", "mode" }, ... ],
      "update": [ { "name", "dst", "changes": { "owner"|"group"|"mode": {"from","to"} } }, ... ],
      "remove": [ { "name", "dst" }, ... ]
    },
    "env": {
      "create": [ { "name", "path", "owner", "group", "mode", "environmentVariable" }, ... ],
      "update": [ { "name", "path", "changes": {"environmentVariable": {"from","to"}} }, ... ],
      "remove": [ { "name", "path" }, ... ]
    },
    "symlink": {
      "create": [ { "name", "path", "target" }, ... ]
    }
  }
`materialize`/`env` each mirror bin/ubx-etc's own create/update/remove
split (metadata-only diffing -- see "Why content is never diffed here"
below); `dst`/`path` are always the concrete filesystem paths
bin/ubx-secrets-apply is expected to act on, verbatim -- it never
recomputes them. Every list is sorted by `name` (ties broken by `path`
where relevant) for a byte-identical plan across repeated runs against
identical inputs -- this project's standing determinism rule (see
nix/users.nix's own "Determinism" section for the general principle this
mirrors).

-- Why content is never diffed here -----------------------------------------

Unlike bin/ubx-etc's own `plan` (which compares a target sha256 against an
observed one), this planner has NO WAY to know whether a secret's actual
BYTES changed: computing that would mean either hashing real secret
material at eval time (nix/secrets.nix's own header explains why that,
too, is refused -- "no secret material ever enters a store object") or
this script reading real secret material itself merely to plan (this
script is exercised entirely with zero-privilege fixtures in tests, and
real secret files are root-only 0400 by design -- SPEC.md §8.1). Content
freshness is instead the EXECUTOR's problem to not worry about at all: per
SPEC.md §8.1, `/run/secrets` is tmpfs, "re-materialized each boot/switch
from the decrypted working tree" -- bin/ubx-secrets-apply always
(re)installs a secret's bytes for every `create`/`update` action this
planner emits, and metadata-only drift (an owner/group/mode disagreement)
is exactly the one thing observable without touching material at all, so
it is exactly what this planner diffs.

-- What counts as "managed" -------------------------------------------------

Exactly bin/ubx-users' own posture (see that script's header, "What counts
as managed"): this planner only ever looks at (1) declared secrets and (2)
whatever `--observed` reports for names IT was told about (never everything
under a real `/run/secrets` -- e.g. it never inspects `--run-secrets-dir`
itself; `observe`, not `plan`, does that walk). A canonical copy present in
`--observed` but absent from the declared manifest is `materialize.remove`
(SPEC.md §7: managed-domain removal is a real converge action here, unlike
bin/ubx-etc's own machine-local-exception carve-out -- there is no
equivalent "never touch this path" concept for secrets, since every
`/run/secrets/<name>` entry is, by construction, either declared or stale).
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import sys

PROG = "ubx-secrets"

# See nix/secrets.nix's own `nameRe` comment: a secret's declared name is a
# plain Nix attribute identifier (SPEC.md §8.1's own `proToken`/`apiToken`/
# `wgKey` example), not a Unix account name -- deliberately NOT
# bin/ubx-users' lowercase-only NAME_RE.
NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$")
MODE_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-7]{3,4}$")
OWNER_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z_][a-z0-9_-]*$")
ENV_VAR_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$")

# The CLOSED field allowlist a manifest secret object may ever carry -- see
# this file's header, "THE ABSOLUTE INVARIANT". Anything else (in
# particular a "src"/"value"/"material"/"content" key -- the shapes a
# tampered or hand-crafted manifest.json might smuggle real secret bytes or
# a store-forcing path through) is refused outright by `validate_manifest`.
ALLOWED_SECRET_KEYS = frozenset(
    {"name", "owner", "group", "mode", "dst", "environmentVariable"}
)


def die(msg):
    print(f"{PROG}: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def load_json(path, default):
    if path is None:
        return default
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
        return json.load(f)


def write_json(obj, out_path):
    text = json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    if out_path is None:
        sys.stdout.write(text)
        return
    tmp = out_path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, out_path)


def canonical_dst(name):
    return f"/run/secrets/{name}"


# -- manifest validation ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Defense-in-depth, independent of nix/secrets.nix's own eval-time checks
# (this script's tests hand-craft manifest.json fixtures directly, with no
# `nix` binary involved at all -- see this file's header).


def validate_manifest(manifest):
    errors = []
    if not isinstance(manifest, dict):
        return ["manifest top level is not a JSON object"]
    if manifest.get("version") != 1:
        errors.append(f"manifest 'version' must be 1, got {manifest.get('version')!r}")

    secrets = manifest.get("secrets")
    if not isinstance(secrets, list):
        errors.append("manifest 'secrets' must be a list")
        secrets = []

    seen_names = set()
    seen_dsts = {}
    for i, s in enumerate(secrets):
        label = f"secrets[{i}]"
        if not isinstance(s, dict):
            errors.append(f"{label} is not an object")
            continue

        extra_keys = sorted(set(s) - ALLOWED_SECRET_KEYS)
        if extra_keys:
            errors.append(
                f"{label} carries disallowed key(s) {extra_keys!r} -- only "
                f"{sorted(ALLOWED_SECRET_KEYS)!r} are permitted (no secret "
                "material or store-forcing path may travel through this "
                "manifest -- SPEC.md §8.1's absolute invariant)"
            )

        name = s.get("name")
        label = f"secrets[{i}] ({name!r})"
        if not isinstance(name, str) or not NAME_RE.match(name):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'name' is not a valid secret name (must match {NAME_RE.pattern})")
        elif name in seen_names:
            errors.append(f"duplicate declared secret name: {name!r}")
        else:
            seen_names.add(name)

        owner = s.get("owner")
        if not isinstance(owner, str) or not OWNER_RE.match(owner):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'owner' must be a valid user name, got {owner!r}")

        group = s.get("group")
        if not isinstance(group, str) or not OWNER_RE.match(group):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'group' must be a valid group name, got {group!r}")

        mode = s.get("mode")
        if not isinstance(mode, str) or not MODE_RE.match(mode):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'mode' must be a 3-4 digit octal string, got {mode!r}")

        dst = s.get("dst")
        if not isinstance(dst, str) or not dst.startswith("/"):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'dst' must be an absolute path string, got {dst!r}")
        elif dst in seen_dsts:
            errors.append(
                f"duplicate effective dst {dst!r} declared by {seen_dsts[dst]!r} and {name!r}"
            )
        else:
            seen_dsts[dst] = name

        env_var = s.get("environmentVariable")
        if env_var is not None and (not isinstance(env_var, str) or not ENV_VAR_RE.match(env_var)):
            errors.append(f"{label} 'environmentVariable' must be null or a valid env var name, got {env_var!r}")

    return errors


def validate_observed(observed):
    errors = []
    if not isinstance(observed, dict):
        return ["observed state top level is not a JSON object"], []
    if observed.get("version") != 1:
        errors.append(f"observed 'version' must be 1, got {observed.get('version')!r}")
    entries = observed.get("entries")
    if not isinstance(entries, list):
        errors.append("observed 'entries' must be a list")
        entries = []
    for i, e in enumerate(entries):
        if not isinstance(e, dict) or not isinstance(e.get("name"), str):
            errors.append(f"observed entries[{i}] is not an object with a string 'name'")
    return errors, entries


# -- the planner --------------------------------------------------------------


def build_plan(manifest, observed_entries):
    declared = {s["name"]: s for s in manifest["secrets"]}
    observed = {e["name"]: e for e in observed_entries}

    mat_create, mat_update, mat_remove = [], [], []
    env_create, env_update, env_remove = [], [], []
    symlink_create = []

    for name in sorted(declared):
        d = declared[name]
        canon = canonical_dst(name)
        obs = observed.get(name)

        if obs is None:
            mat_create.append({
                "name": name, "dst": canon,
                "owner": d["owner"], "group": d["group"], "mode": d["mode"],
            })
        else:
            changes = {}
            for field in ("owner", "group", "mode"):
                if d[field] != obs.get(field):
                    changes[field] = {"from": obs.get(field), "to": d[field]}
            if changes:
                mat_update.append({"name": name, "dst": canon, "changes": changes})

        declared_var = d.get("environmentVariable")
        observed_var = obs.get("envVar") if obs is not None else None
        env_path = f"{canon}.env"
        if declared_var is not None and observed_var is None:
            env_create.append({
                "name": name, "path": env_path,
                "owner": d["owner"], "group": d["group"], "mode": "0400",
                "environmentVariable": declared_var,
            })
        elif declared_var is not None and observed_var is not None and declared_var != observed_var:
            env_update.append({
                "name": name, "path": env_path,
                "changes": {"environmentVariable": {"from": observed_var, "to": declared_var}},
            })
        elif declared_var is None and observed_var is not None:
            env_remove.append({"name": name, "path": env_path})

        # -- symlink: only when the effective dst differs from the
        # canonical copy (this file's header, "The canonical-copy model").
        # An already-correct symlink (observed symlinkTarget == canon) is a
        # real no-op, not re-planned -- see this file's header on
        # `--manifest` in `observe`'s own docstring for how that
        # observation is produced.
        if d["dst"] != canon:
            current_target = obs.get("symlinkTarget") if obs is not None else None
            if current_target != canon:
                symlink_create.append({"name": name, "path": d["dst"], "target": canon})

    for name in sorted(observed):
        if name not in declared:
            mat_remove.append({"name": name, "dst": canonical_dst(name)})

    empty = not (
        mat_create or mat_update or mat_remove
        or env_create or env_update or env_remove
        or symlink_create
    )

    return {
        "version": 1,
        "empty": empty,
        "materialize": {
            "create": sorted(mat_create, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
            "update": sorted(mat_update, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
            "remove": sorted(mat_remove, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
        },
        "env": {
            "create": sorted(env_create, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
            "update": sorted(env_update, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
            "remove": sorted(env_remove, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
        },
        "symlink": {
            "create": sorted(symlink_create, key=lambda x: x["name"]),
        },
    }


def cmd_plan(args):
    manifest = load_json(args.manifest, None)
    if manifest is None:
        die("--manifest is required")
    m_errors = validate_manifest(manifest)
    if m_errors:
        die("manifest failed validation:\n" + "\n".join(f"  - {e}" for e in m_errors))

    observed = load_json(args.observed, {"version": 1, "entries": []})
    o_errors, entries = validate_observed(observed)
    if o_errors:
        die("observed state failed validation:\n" + "\n".join(f"  - {e}" for e in o_errors))

    plan = build_plan(manifest, entries)
    write_json(plan, args.out)
    sys.exit(0)


# -- observe: real (or fixture) /run/secrets -> observed-state JSON ---------
#
# See this file's header, "The observed schema". Regular files only (a
# `.env` sibling is folded into its base entry, never emitted as its own
# entry); anything else (a directory, a dangling name) is silently skipped
# -- `plan` above never needs to know about anything this walk doesn't
# already understand how to describe.


def read_env_var_name(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            line = f.readline().rstrip("\n")
    except OSError:
        return None
    if "=" not in line:
        return None
    return line.split("=", 1)[0] or None


def observe_run_secrets(run_secrets_dir):
    entries = []
    if not os.path.isdir(run_secrets_dir):
        return entries
    for fname in sorted(os.listdir(run_secrets_dir)):
        if fname.endswith(".env"):
            continue
        fpath = os.path.join(run_secrets_dir, fname)
        if not os.path.isfile(fpath) or os.path.islink(fpath):
            continue
        st = os.stat(fpath)
        entry = {
            "name": fname,
            "owner": _uid_name(st.st_uid),
            "group": _gid_name(st.st_gid),
            "mode": format(st.st_mode & 0o7777, "04o"),
            "envVar": read_env_var_name(fpath + ".env") if os.path.isfile(fpath + ".env") else None,
            "symlinkTarget": None,
        }
        entries.append(entry)
    return entries


def _uid_name(uid):
    try:
        import pwd
        return pwd.getpwuid(uid).pw_name
    except (ImportError, KeyError, OSError):
        return str(uid)


def _gid_name(gid):
    try:
        import grp
        return grp.getgrgid(gid).gr_name
    except (ImportError, KeyError, OSError):
        return str(gid)


def cmd_observe(args):
    entries = observe_run_secrets(args.run_secrets_dir)

    if args.manifest is not None:
        manifest = load_json(args.manifest, None)
        by_name = {e["name"]: e for e in entries}
        for s in manifest.get("secrets", []):
            name = s.get("name")
            canon = canonical_dst(name)
            dst = s.get("dst")
            if dst is None or dst == canon:
                continue
            target = None
            if os.path.islink(dst):
                try:
                    target = os.path.realpath(dst)
                except OSError:
                    target = None
            if name in by_name:
                by_name[name]["symlinkTarget"] = target
            # If this secret has no canonical entry yet (never
            # materialized), there is nothing to attach a symlinkTarget
            # onto -- `plan`'s own `materialize.create` branch will fire
            # regardless, and `symlink.create` fires too since a null
            # current_target never equals a real canon path.

    write_json({"version": 1, "entries": entries}, args.out)
    sys.exit(0)


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog=PROG,
        description=(
            "Secrets-primitive convergence planner and observed-state "
            "walker (SPEC.md §8.1, §4.3 'none' downtime; issue #78, "
            "milestone M4)."
        ),
    )
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    p_plan = sub.add_parser("plan", help="compute a convergence plan from a manifest + observed state")
    p_plan.add_argument("--manifest", required=True, help="declared secrets manifest (nix/secrets.nix's renderManifestJSON output)")
    p_plan.add_argument("--observed", default=None, help="observed /run/secrets state JSON (default: assume nothing materialized yet)")
    p_plan.add_argument("--out", default=None, help="write the plan here instead of stdout")
    p_plan.set_defaults(func=cmd_plan)

    p_obs = sub.add_parser("observe", help="walk a real (or fixture) /run/secrets directory and emit its observed-state JSON")
    p_obs.add_argument("--run-secrets-dir", default="/run/secrets", dest="run_secrets_dir", help="directory to walk (default: /run/secrets)")
    p_obs.add_argument("--manifest", default=None, help="optional declared manifest, to also resolve custom-dst symlink targets (see this script's header)")
    p_obs.add_argument("--out", default=None, help="write the observed state here instead of stdout")
    p_obs.set_defaults(func=cmd_observe)

    args = parser.parse_args()
    try:
        args.func(args)
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:
        die(str(e))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
